{"author":{"id":"b28ace64b4a52eef863f0423a2df7021241dd0c0bac0a20931e2333fd3a1b77e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794738541,"nonce":"gP0e+5Z4xThT8RqycnfWS064cNI=","message":"Fixed.\n\n**Change** (`src/client/factory.js`, CSS block):\n\n```css\n/* before */\n.gb-btn-primary{background:var(--dsw-alias-brand-primary,#4a6cf7);border-color:transparent;color:#fff}\n/* after */\n.gb-btn-primary{background:var(--dsw-alias-button-primary-fill,#4a6cf7);border-color:transparent;color:var(--dsw-alias-label-primary-foreground,#fff)}\n.gb-btn-primary:hover:not(:disabled){background:var(--dsw-alias-button-primary-hover,#3a5be0)}\n```\n\nWhy this works, for both palettes:\n\n| token | light | dark |\n|---|---|---|\n| `--dsw-alias-button-primary-fill` (= brand-primary) | bluish-1000 (dark navy) | bluish-50 `rgb(249,250,251)` |\n| `--dsw-alias-label-primary-foreground` | bluish-00 (white) | bluish-1000 `rgb(15,17,21)` |\n\nSo the label now follows the fill in every theme instead of being hardcoded `#fff`. The dedicated `:hover` rule (same `0,3,0` specificity as `.gb-btn:hover:not(:disabled)`, declared later) keeps the primary hover fill instead of collapsing to the translucent `.gb-btn` hover — the state in which the bug was hidden. Token names and pairing match DSH's own `ui-primitives` `Button.module.css` (`.primary`), so the plugin stays consistent with the shell.\n\n**Verification**\n- `node --check src/client/factory.js` — OK.\n- `node scripts/build-client.mjs` — rebuilt `lib/client.js` (23812 chars).\n- `node --test \"tests/*.test.mjs\"` — 39/39 pass.\n- Serving check against the live GUI: `GET http://127.0.0.1:3081/plugins/dsh-git-bug/client.js` returns the bundle with the corrected rules.\n\nAffects both primary buttons in the panel: the toolbar \"+ New Issue\" toggle and the CreateForm \"Create\" submit.\n\n**Note:** the running GUI (http://127.0.0.1:3081) needs a page refresh to load the rebuilt browser bundle.","files":null}]}